QuestGuidance.Register("en",81,{
[2561]="7001BEA2\n1\tBurn banner at Mokûrz Gundul and defeat Nákurz\tMokûrz Gundul lies to the north from Talan Fanuidhol. Maenhador has asked you to burn the Orc-banner at Mokûrz Gundul and defeat the camp's champion.\n2\tTalk to Maenhador at Talan Fanuidhol\tMaenhador is at Talan Fanuidhol, south of Mokûrz Gundul. You should return to Maenhador with the tidings of your victory at Mokûrz Gundul.\n",
[2562]="7001BEA3\n1\tBurn banner at Nardur-stazg and defeat Narash\tNardur-stazg lies to the north-west from Talan Gwilith. Raingon has asked you to burn the Orc-banner at Nardur-stazg and defeat the camp's champion. Note: While Fanuidhol Defence is active, Raingon will not be available for quest completion or comments. You will have to wait for Fanuidhol Defence to end to complete this quest.\n2\tTalk to Raingon at Talan Gwilith\tRaingon is at Talan Gwilith, south-east of Nardur-stazg. You should return to Raingon with the tidings of your victory at Nardur-stazg. Note: While Fanuidhol Defence is active, Raingon will not be available for quest completion or comments. You will have to wait for Fanuidhol Defence to end to complete this quest.\n",
[2563]="70027208\n1\tBurn crates of supplies (total: 3)\tCrates of supplies can be found in Upper Barnavon. Lhur has asked you to enter Upper Barnavon and burn the supplies Madin Brenin's men have gathered for Saruman's war efforts.\n2\tTalk to Lhur in Barnavon\tLhur is in Lower Barnavon. You should return to Lhur with news of your success.\n",
[2564]="70037166\n1\tYou should use nearby torches to burn the barricades at the gates of Torsbury.\t\n2\tUse torch to burn the first barricade\030Use torch to burn the second barricade\030Use torch to burn the third barricade\030Use torch to burn the fourth barricade\tBarricades and torches can be found and the south-east and south-west gates of Torsbury. You should use nearby torches to burn the barricades at the gates of Torsbury.\n",
[2565]="7001BBAE\n1\tThe corpses of the Eglain who failed to escape the spiders lie in the gorge beneath Minas Eriol. Hunulf Munce asked that you burn the corpses of the slain Eglain beneath Minas Eriol.\t\n2\tTalk to Hunulf Munce\tHunulf Munce is at his encampment on the far eastern side of Minas Eriol. You found several of the slain Eglain and burned their bodies. You should now return to Hunulf.\n",
[2566]="7002BFFB\n1\tBurn banners of the Great Eye at Lashkarg (total: 6)\tBanners of the Great Eye can be found at Lashkarg, south-east of Etheburg in the Brown Lands. Dagbert asked you to enter Lashkarg and burn the banners of the Great Eye.\n2\tTalk to Dagbert at Etheburg in the Brown Lands\tDagbert is at Etheburg in the Brown Lands, north-west of Lashkarg. You should return to Dagbert with news of your success.\n",
[2567]="7002EA47\n1\tBurn banners of the Great Eye at Lashkarg (total: 6)\tBanners of the Great Eye can be found at Lashkarg, south-east of Etheburg in the Brown Lands. Céola asked you to enter Lashkarg and burn the banners of the Great Eye.\n2\tTalk to Céola at Etheburg in the Brown Lands\tCéola is at Etheburg in the Brown Lands, north-west of Lashkarg. You should return to Céola with news of your success.\n",
[2568]="7004BEBA\n1\tDestroy tents at Fushaum Bal South (total: 8)\tFushaum Bal is located in Talath Úrui. You should destroy tents in Fushaum Bal South.\n2\tCompleted\tDestroyed many tents at Fushaum Bal South.\n",
[2569]="7003A005\n1\tDestroy the supply waggons\tThere are supply waggons throughout the camp of the Boar-tribe Orcs. You should destroy the waggons of the Boar-tribe Orcs in order to hinder their supply efforts.\n2\tDestroy supply waggons (total: 3)\tThere are supply waggons throughout the camp of the Boar-tribe Orcs. You should destroy the waggons of the Boar-tribe Orcs in order to hinder their war-efforts.\n3\tCompleted\tWith the supply waggons destroyed, the Boar-tribe Orcs will be hard-pressed to restock.\n",
[2570]="7004DCE5\n1\tUse Barrel-rack\tBarrel-racks can be found throughout the Hall Under the Mountain. Snállar has asked you to knock on various barrels of ale to try to expose the ale-thieves in Erebor.\n2\tTalk to Snállar\tSnállar can be found in the Hall Under the Mountain. You have driven off several ale-soaked cave-claws in the Hall Under the Mountain and should now return to Snállar.\n",
[2571]="7000BFFF\n1\tCollect scales from Fissure-worms\t\n2\tBring the Fissure-worm Scales to Thorgest\030Collect Fissure-worm Scale (total: 12)\tThe worm-caves are to the south-east of Thorgest's dwelling. Fissure-worm scales look like they would make strong armour for the Elves of Rivendell.\n",
[2572]="70044D53\n1\tTravel to the Blue Theatre in the Fourth Circle\tThe Blue Theatre can be found to the south in the Fourth Circle of Minas Tirith. Polla has asked you to meet her and the rest of the Cloudyheads in the Blue Theatre as they work to prepare their performance.\n2\tTalk to someone from the Cloudyheads inside the Blue Theatre\tMembers of the Cloudyheads can be found inside the Blue Theatre in the Fourth Circle of Minas Tirith. You have arrived at the Blue Theatre and should now speak to someone from the Cloudyheads about what is to be done next.\n3\tTalk to Fróki in the Blue Theatre\tFróki can be found inside the Blue Theatre at the southern end of the Fourth Circle. Fróki has asked you to help The Cloudyheads prepare for their performance in the Blue Theatre.\n4\tTalk to Polla Stoutley in the Blue Theatre\tPolla Stoutley and the Cloudyheads can be found inside the Blue Theatre to the far right of the entrance in an alcove with a fire-place. You have helped the Cloudyheads perform inside the Blue Theatre, and should now speak to Polla Stoutley.\n",
[2573]="70019389\n1\tCollect berries (total: 8)\030Collect button mushrooms (total: 8)\tMushrooms can be found along the bank of the stream that borders Imlad Lalaith. Berries can be found in the forest north of Imlad Lalaith. Aesbrennil would like you to gather berries and button-like mushrooms for the meal she is preparing for the evening festivities.\n2\tTalk to Aesbrennil at the Vineyards of Lórien\tAesbrennil is at the Vineyards of Lórien, south of Imlad Lalaith. You should bring the mushrooms and berries back to Aesbrennil.\n",
[2574]="7004DA23\n1\tDefeat fire-flies or sickle-flies in Eryn Lasgalen and the Dale-lands (total: 10)\tFire-flies can be found in Eryn Lasgalen. Sickle-flies can be found in the Dale-lands. You should defeat fire-flies and sickle-flies in Eryn Lasgalen and the Dale-lands.\n2\tCompleted\tYou have defeated many flies in Eryn Lasgalen and the Dale-lands.\n",
[2575]="7005B910\n1\tDestroy wasp nests (total: 8)\030Defeat Clovengap fire-flies (total: 6)\030Defeat Clovengap hornets (total: 10)\tThe wasp hive can be found in south-western Clovengap. Borghild has asked you to deal with the wasp infestation in the nearby ruins.\n2\tReturn to Borghild\tBorghild is in western Clovengap. You should let Borghild know that you have completed the task of defeating the wasps.\n",
[2576]="700005E9\n1\tFind Gil Sandheaver's walking tree\tWalt Whitrose mentioned that Gil Sandheaver had come from the north and east, where the lake meets the woodland. Walt Whitrose believes it is worth looking into Gil Sandheaver's claims that trees were walking near Nen Harn, if for no other reason that Gil's peace of mind.\n2\tTalk to Walt Whitrose in Nen Harn\tWalt Whitrose is at his camp on the western edge of Nen Harn. Your discovery should be explained to Walt Whitrose at his camp, if only to warn him that such things exist out here in the northernmost parts of Bree-land.\n3\tTalk to Gil Sandheaver at the Hengstacer Farm\tGil Sandheaver is at the Hengstacer Farm, west of Walt Whitrose's camp at Nen Harn and north of Bree-town. Walt Whitrose told you to take news of your victory to Gil Sandheaver, with the reassurance that he may once again walk the woods in peace.\n",
[2577]="700372D1\n1\tCollect Huorn acorns (total: 8)\tHuorn acorns can be found throughout the eaves of Fangorn, bordering the Broadacres. Blackthorn asked you to gather Huorn acorns to summon his Huorns with.\n2\tPlace Huorn acorns (total: 8)\tThere are places to summon Huorns throughout the eaves of Fangorn, bordering the Broadacres. Blackthorn asked you to put the acorns in special places to summon the Huorns.\n3\tTalk to Blackthorn\tBlackthorn awaits your return in the eaves of Fangorn, bordering the Broadacres. You should return to Blackthorn and let him know that you have done as he asked.\n",
[2578]="700372DB\n1\tCollect Huorn acorns (total: 8)\tHuorn acorns can be found throughout the eaves of Fangorn, bordering the Broadacres. Blackthorn asked you to gather Huorn acorns to summon his Huorns with.\n2\tThere are places to summon Huorns throughout the eaves of Fangorn, bordering the Broadacres. Blackthorn asked you to put the acorns in special places to summon the Huorns.\t\n3\tTalk to Blackthorn\tBlackthorn awaits your return in the eaves of Fangorn, bordering the Broadacres. You should return to Blackthorn and let him know that you have done as he asked.\n",
[2579]="7000003C\n1\tBring boar-bones and boar-feet to Arinora\030Collect boar leg-bones (total: 8)\030Collect boar-feet (total: 8)\tBoars can be found in the area surrounding The Forsaken Inn and north-east among the Weather Hills. Arinora asked you to collect boar-feet and leg-bones for a dish she serves at The Forsaken Inn.\n",
[2580]="70000006\n1\tTalk to Shirriff Robin Smallburrow\tShirriff Robin Smallburrow can be found inside the Ivy Bush in the centre of Hobbiton. Since it will be three months before Hyacinth Took can have more fireworks ready for Lobelia Sackville-Baggins, a month too late for her party, Lobelia instructed you to speak with Robin Smallburrow about recovering Hyacinth's stolen fireworks.\n2\tTalk to Thain Paladin Took II\tThe Thain can be found at the Great Smials in Tuckborough, south of Hobbiton. Lobelia Sackville-Baggins sent you to speak with Robin Smallburrow about Hyacinth Took's stolen fireworks, but Shirriff Smallburrow told you the matter was outside of his jurisdiction. He suggested you speak with Paladin Took, Thain of the Shire.\n",
[2581]="70040ECE\n1\tDefeat Corsair patrol-leaders (total: 4)\tCorsair patrol-leaders can be found along the roadways to the north and north-east of Ost Lontir. Gilanor has asked you to clear the roadways of Corsair patrols in hopes of protecting the people of Ost Lontir.\n2\tTalk to Gilanor\tGilanor can be found in Ost Lontir in central Belfalas. You have defeated many roaming Corsairs and should report your success to Gilanor.\n",
[2582]="70042F63\n1\tDefeat Haradrim and Easterling forces within Osgiliath (total: 16)\tHaradrim and Easterling forces can be found in eastern Osgiliath. Damrod has asked you to seek out and defeat Haradrim and Easterling forces in Osgiliath.\n2\tTalk to Damrod in the culverts of Osgiliath\tDamrod can be found in the culverts of Osgiliath. You have defeated many of the Haradrim and Easterling forces and should now return to Damrod.\n",
[2583]="700509C7\n1\tDefeat Bánbros, Scourge of Óinsbridge\tBánbros poses a great threat to all that enter Óinsbridge.\n2\tDefeat Bánbros, Scourge of Óinsbridge\tBánbros poses a great threat to all that enter Óinsbridge.\n3\tCompleted\tBánbros poses a great threat to all that enter Óinsbridge.\n",
[2584]="7000D4F2\n1\tMinas Caul is one of the large towers of Barad Gúlaran, south of Gath Forthnír. You must travel to Barad Gúlaran and issue a challenge to Bâlak, the emissary of the White-hand, inside Minas Caul.\t\n2\tTalk to Brúnfair\tBrúnfair is at Gath Forthnír, north of Barad Gúlaran. Having defeated Bâlak, you should return to Gath Forthnir and tell Brúnfair that you have accomplished the deed.\n",
[2585]="70054D78\n1\tDefeat Manôzagar\tDefeat Manôzagar within Mokh Núlum, the Vault of Anguish.\n2\tDefeat Narkhor the Flensed\tDefeat Agath-kali's guardian, Narkhor the Flensed.\n3\tFind Morloth and interrupt the Rite of Returning\tTûm Morloth can be found outside Bâr Nírnaeth, the Houses of Lamentation. Agath-kali has absconded to Tûm Morloth to begin her final preparations for Dhak Thrakrut, the Rite of Returning.\n4\tDefeat Agath-kali, the Mistress of Lamentation\tAgath-kali can be found in Tûm Morloth. You must defeat Agath-kali before she can perform Dhak Thrakrut, the Rite of Returning.\n",
[2586]="70054D7B\n1\tDefeat Manôzagar\tDefeat Manôzagar within Mokh Núlum, the Vault of Anguish.\n2\tDefeat Narkhor the Flensed\tDefeat Agath-kali's guardian, Narkhor the Flensed.\n3\tFind Morloth and interrupt the Rite of Returning\tTûm Morloth can be found outside Bâr Nírnaeth, the Houses of Lamentation. Agath-kali has absconded to Tûm Morloth to begin her final preparations for Dhak Thrakrut, the Rite of Returning.\n4\tDefeat Agath-kali, the Mistress of Lamentation\tAgath-kali can be found in Tûm Morloth. You must defeat Agath-kali before she can perform Dhak Thrakrut, the Rite of Returning.\n",
[2587]="70054D79\n1\tDefeat Manôzagar\tDefeat Manôzagar within Mokh Núlum, the Vault of Anguish.\n2\tDefeat Narkhor the Flensed\tDefeat Agath-kali's guardian, Narkhor the Flensed.\n3\tFind Morloth and interrupt the Rite of Returning\tTûm Morloth can be found outside Bâr Nírnaeth, the Houses of Lamentation. Agath-kali has absconded to Tûm Morloth to begin her final preparations for Dhak Thrakrut, the Rite of Returning.\n4\tDefeat Agath-kali, the Mistress of Lamentation\tAgath-kali can be found in Tûm Morloth. You must defeat Agath-kali before she can perform Dhak Thrakrut, the Rite of Returning.\n",
[2588]="70054D7A\n1\tDefeat Manôzagar\tDefeat Manôzagar within Mokh Núlum, the Vault of Anguish.\n2\tDefeat Narkhor the Flensed\tDefeat Agath-kali's guardian, Narkhor the Flensed.\n3\tFind Morloth and interrupt the Rite of Returning\tTûm Morloth can be found outside Bâr Nírnaeth, the Houses of Lamentation. Agath-kali has absconded to Tûm Morloth to begin her final preparations for Dhak Thrakrut, the Rite of Returning.\n4\tDefeat Agath-kali, the Mistress of Lamentation\tAgath-kali can be found in Tûm Morloth. You must defeat Agath-kali before she can perform Dhak Thrakrut, the Rite of Returning.\n",
[2589]="7002C60C\n1\tRescue Bíli\tYou should find Bíli the dwarf and help him get back to the mill. Armund suggested that Bíli might have been exploring somewhere not far to the east of the old sawmill in the Limlight Gorge.\n2\tTalk to Bíli\tYou should speak with Bíli at the Limlight Gorge sawmill.\n",
[2590]="70054798\n1\tDestroy the dark forges\tBúrzangh, the Shrouded Forge, can be found in the Circle of Sorrow in Minas Morgul. You should destroy the dark forges.\n2\tDestroy the dark forges (total: 10)\tBúrzangh, the Shrouded Forge, can be found in the Circle of Sorrow in Minas Morgul. You should destroy the dark forges.\n3\tCompleted\tDestroy many dark forges in Búrzangh.\n",
[2591]="70054799\n1\tDestroy the forsaken coal\tBúrzangh, the Shrouded Forge, can be found in the Circle of Sorrow in Minas Morgul. You should destroy the forsaken coal.\n2\tDestroy the forsaken coal (total: 12)\tBúrzangh, the Shrouded Forge, can be found in the Circle of Sorrow in Minas Morgul. You should destroy the forsaken coal.\n3\tCompleted\tYou have destroyed much of the forsaken coal within Búrzangh.\n",
[2592]="70054796\n1\tDefeat foes within the Shrouded Forge\tBúrzangh, the Shrouded Forge, can be found in the Circle of Sorrow in Minas Morgul. You should defeat those within the Shrouded Forge.\n2\tDefeat foes within the Shrouded Forge (total: 12)\tBúrzangh, the Shrouded Forge, can be found in the Circle of Sorrow in Minas Morgul. You should defeat those within the Shrouded Forge.\n3\tCompleted\tYou have defeated many foes within the Shrouded Forge.\n",
